course: dictionary
lesson: 8031
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. Context tells you which meaning the writer wants. Read the words around the word and ask: which meaning fits here?
explain: «In the middle is a dish of tarts that look so good that Alice wishes they'd hurry up and hand round the refreshments.» You hand round tarts and drinks to guests, so refreshments means small amounts of food and drink here.
explain: Refreshment (no s) can mean something different: the feeling of being fresh and rested again after being tired, hot or thirsty. To check, swap your meaning into the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have found the right one.
fact: Refreshments, with an s, means small amounts of food and drink at a meeting, show or party.
fact: Refreshment, without an s, can mean the feeling of being fresh and rested again after being tired, hot or thirsty.
fact: You may see the phrases «light refreshments», «refreshments will be served» and «a refreshment stand».
fact: A refreshment stand is a small place where food and drinks are sold.
fact: Context clues, such as the words around the word, tell you which meaning to choose.
exercise: «Refreshments will be served after the sports day.» What are refreshments here? | Games and races for the crowd | Prizes for the winners | *Small amounts of food and drink | A rest from lessons for the day
exercise: After a hot, long walk, a cold drink gave Sam refreshment. What does refreshment mean? | *The feeling of being fresh and rested again | A plate of tarts for the party | A new pair of trainers | A loud noise made by the crowd
exercise: In «Alice wishes they'd hurry up and hand round the refreshments», what is being handed round? | Letters to the head teacher | Umbrellas for the rain | *Food and drink for the guests | Maths homework
test: «Refreshments will be served at the school fête.» Does refreshments mean food and drink, or the feeling of being rested? | A kind of school game | *Food and drink | The feeling of being rested | A rest from lessons
test: «After the long bike ride, the cold water was pure refreshment.» What does refreshment mean here? | *The feeling of being fresh and rested again | Small amounts of food at a party | A bike repair | A stall that sells tickets
exam: Ella says refreshment and refreshments are the same word with the same meaning. Is she right? | No, refreshment is only the name of a shop | Yes, they always mean exactly the same thing | Yes, but only at a party | *No, the s changes the meaning: refreshments usually means food and drink, and refreshment usually means feeling fresh again
